# Magma Oceans – early in a body’s history

On some bodies\, all \(or some\) of the outer part of the planet may have been melted  __early in its history__

This model

links basalt & anorthosite on the Moon:

Basalt ‘sinks’ & anorthosite ‘floats’

Allows substantial differentiation to occur in the magmas – required to form lunar KREEP \(Potassium\, Rare Earth Elements & Phosphorus rich magmas\)

Unmelted part might be either never melted or crystal ‘cumulates’

![](images/PK/PK4LM_76.png)

::: {.notes}

Moon very active in early history, less active later

Surface of planet was entirely melted – magma ocean

Plagioclase floated and collected on far side of ocean

KREEP – K, REE, P rich magmas explained by this model

