# Tectonics Features Beyond Earth

![](images/PK/PK4LM_117.jpg)

<span style="color:#0070c0">Tectonic features on Mercury</span>



* Evidence for faulting
  * i\.e\. tectonic activity – likely cracking in surface
  * \(not plate tectonics\)


![](images/PK/PK4LM_118.png)

![](images/PK/PK4LM_119.jpg)

::: {.notes}

Faulting mostly due to tidal stresses due to being close to the sun
Don’t get plate tectonics
Extensional and compressional faults

:::

![](images/PK/PK4LM_120.jpg)

Tectonic features on Mars

\(McSween et al\. 2019\)

::: {.notes}

Modern tectonics of Mars is mostly compressional faults
Probably due to cooling
Most features are probably very old


:::

Tectonic features on Mars

![](images/PK/PK4LM_121.jpg)

![](images/PK/PK4LM_122.jpg)

Graben are formed by extensional stresses \(red arrows\) in the crust\. Graben consist of flat\-floored valleys bound by opposite\-facing normal faults\, and are often separated by upland blocks called horsts\.

Mars: Simple graben and horsts in Tantalus Fossae on eastern flank of Alba Mons\. Line of pit craters suggests drainage into subsurface voids\, possibly created by tension cracks \(THEMIS IR daytime mosaic\)\. NASA/JPL\, Arizona State University\.

::: {.notes}

Extensional faults forming horsts and grabens
Inflation of crust beneath the volcano as magma was injected beneath it, stretched the surface and caused extensional faults
Canberra region of horsts and grabens – like what we saw at Lake George

:::

<span style="color:#0070c0">Tectonic features on Mars</span>

